Provenance
================================================================================

Substantial portions of this software were extracted from the Design Room of:

    github.com/ibuilder/massing
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Matthew M. Emma

Both projects are MIT and share a copyright holder, so the extraction carries no
licensing condition beyond retaining the notice above — which is what this file
does. It exists anyway, because the audience for it is an enterprise legal
reviewer asking "where did this code come from", and the honest answer should be
one file away rather than reconstructed from commit archaeology.

Every extracted file carries a header naming its origin path and the upstream
commit it was taken from:

    Extracted from ibuilder/massing @ <sha> (apps/web/src/viewer/snapEngine.ts), MIT.

`docs/PROVENANCE.tsv` is the machine-readable ledger of the same facts, and CI
asserts the two agree in both directions (see scripts/check-provenance.mjs) — a
file with a header and no ledger row fails, and so does a ledger row with no
file. The ledger is also what the weekly divergence report reads to detect
upstream changes to code we extracted.

We deliberately did not import filtered git history. Roughly half of the
extracted code was restructured during the move (a 5,064-line file became six
packages), so `git blame` would break at the move commit regardless, and the
rationale is recorded in docs/adr/0005-clean-history-with-provenance-ledger.md.

